      "books": [
        "main"
      ],
      "pages": [
        {
          "html": "<p class=\"lore-page__header\"><em>A mind incapable of being reprogrammed is a vulnerable one. But you are never more vulnerable when you are being reprogrammed! Whether this is self-inflicted or is done so by your environment is of little consequence. After you&#39;re in a more stable state, can you more closely represent what reality is?</em><span class=\"lore-page__header-by\"><strong>Ether&#39;s Bicentennial address 2247</strong></span></p>\n<p>The sun burned brightly even though it was an early spring day. In particular it seemed the rays of light had chosen a particular person that day, casually sitting on a bench in a small park. Perhaps it was the fact that he stood out particularly against the background. The brightest of green colors around him, against his casual black outfit which blended well with his skin. He remembered not exactly how he got there... by the time he became aware of himself, it seemed an age of the universe had gone by.</p>",
          "refs": [],
          "factIds": []
        }
      ],
      "file": "content/lore/chapters/prologue.md"
    }
